The resumed image has the same target/base gap and also resets the temporary launcher workaround; `lake` cannot identify its executable through the container’s `/proc` view. I’m restoring only that external runtime shim (outside the project and without changing the pinned toolchain), then I’ll use the compiler to validate the definitions and inspect the exact proof boundary again.
